# How to properly use Ant Design with TanStack Start #4052
created: 2025-04-25, last updated: 2026-08-09, [Read more](https://github.com/TanStack/router/discussions/4052)

You want `StyleProvider` + `extractStyle` on the server, injected into head before hydration.
In TanStack Start the cleanest hook is a root-route `head` function that calls `extractStyle(cache, true)` after render — without `true` you only get partial rules.
...
#### 2.
Server entry: extract and inject styles into HTML head
TanStack Start has a server entry point where you can modify the HTML shell:
```
// app/entry-server.tsx
import { createStartHandler, defaultStreamHandler } from '@tanstack/react-start/server';
import { getRouterManifest } from '@tanstack/react-start/router-manifest';
import { createRouter } from './router';
import { extractStyle } from '@ant-design/cssinjs';
export default createStartHandler({
createRouter,
getRouterManifest,
})(async ({ request, router, responseHeaders }) => {
// Wait for streaming to finish so we can extract all rendered styles
const stream = await defaultStreamHandler({ request, router, responseHeaders });
// This won't work directly because the stream is already consumed.
// Instead, use the Document API or a custom HTML wrapper.
return stream;
});

